      "name": "CrowdStrike Uncovers New Prompt Injection Techniques",
      "description": "Microsoft has taken apart a destructive Windows backdoor it calls GigaWiper. What stands out is how it is built: not one tool but three older destructive programs bolted into one, offered as commands the operator can choose from. Each is a different way to break a machine: wipe the whole disk, overwrite the Windows drive, or run fake \"ransomware\" that scrambles files with a key it never saves",
